 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? Of course. What kind of places do you go to? The best thing is a reliable cafe or small local restaurant with good gluten free options. Ask for the menu, and check if they have a gluten free section. Some cafes make their own gluten free bread, which isn't always safe. Soy sauce and miso are usually fine, but check the label. Many soy sauces add barley for flavour, and some miso is made with wheat. Sushi is tricky. Many places can make safe rolls by lining the rice with cornstarch or potato starch, but some use soy sauce mixed into the rice.",
